critical  Mail: SPF ends in +all: every server in the world is allowed to send mail as this domain.
critical  Route: RPKI says invalid_asn: AS64501 is not authorised to announce 198.51.100.0/24. Networks that check drop this route; it can be a hijack.
critical  Route: AS64666 also announced 198.51.100.0/24, until 2026-11-12: a hand-over, or a hijack.
critical  Changes: The origin of the route changed from AS64999 to AS64501 since the last run.
warning  DNS: The zone is not signed: a forged answer cannot be told from a true one.
warning  DNS: The 2 name servers placed are all in one network, AS64500: when it fails, the name stops resolving.
warning  Certificates: The newest certificate in the public logs ends on 2026-11-20.
warning  Route: Every one of the 12 paths seen goes through AS64510: a single point of failure.
warning  Routers: 1 of 2 probes did not reach the site.
warning  Changes: RPKI was valid in the last run and is invalid_asn now.
notice  Mail: DMARC is p=none: forged mail is reported, and still delivered.
notice  IPv6: The name has no IPv6 address.
✓ the alerts of a survey
critical  DNS: The signatures of the zone end in less than three days: after that, resolvers that check them stop answering for the name.
critical  Subdomains: old.example.org is an alias of old-shop.s3.amazonaws.com, which no longer exists at Amazon S3: whoever creates it there serves pages under your name.
critical  Exposure: 2 known vulnerabilities in the software Shodan saw at 198.51.100.7: CVE-2024-0001, CVE-2024-0002. The address is the edge's (Cloudflare), not the server behind it.
warning  DNS: The zone is signed with algorithm 5, which rests on SHA-1; resolvers are dropping it.
warning  DNS: The name server ns2.gone.example has no address: part of the delegation leads nowhere.
warning  Mail: The SPF record needs 12 more questions; receivers stop at ten and then treat it as broken.
warning  Subdomains: lab.example.org is an alias of lab.gone.example, which does not exist.
warning  Site: No HSTS header: a browser's first visit can be sent to plain http and read on the way.
warning  Certificates: A certificate in force was issued by DigiCert, which the CAA records do not name.
warning  Exposure: Port 3389 (Remote Desktop) is open to the whole internet at 198.51.100.7. The address is the edge's (Cloudflare), not the server behind it.
warning  Route: The ROA allows prefixes as long as /24 and /23 is announced: a forged, more specific route would pass as valid.
warning  Route: 198.51.100.0/24, a part of 198.51.100.0/23, is announced by AS64666: routers send it the traffic for those addresses. A customer's block, or a hijack.
notice  Mail: Neither MTA-STS nor DANE: a network in between can make senders deliver the mail of this domain without encryption.
notice  Route: No route object in the routing registries for 198.51.100.0/23 from AS64501: networks that filter by them may refuse the route.
